hey guys i'm vadim with maxtec and as  you probably know there's some drama  going on with the m2 macbook pro so i  think it's time to turn off the  teleprompter no script straight from my  heart explain the entire situation so  you can get a better understanding of  what's going on as well as make some  changes on my end so with that said let  me get into this explanation there is  recently been a lot of people saying  that i am way too negative about the m2  macbook pro specifically on twitter and  now that i look back with everything  that happened i do think that i was  pointing out a lot of the flaws and the  findings that we were finding in our  testing when we were testing all the  different models and variations of the  m2 macbook pro so yes i think i have  been a little bit negative so i'm gonna  try to change that in the future to try  to show more of the positive things  because there are positive things about  the m2 macbook pro yes the m2 chip is  faster especially for the graphics  performance it is a really big  difference and some of the tests we ran  45 faster and i did not talk about that  that much because i was focusing on some  of the other issues that we were finding  with the m2 macbook pro and i actually  got one tweet claiming that there was a  laptop company that's probably paying me  a big check to talk down on apple and to  talk down on the m2 macbook pro which is  obviously not true because for many  years people have been calling me an  apple fanboy an apple chill and they've  claimed that apple is paying me money to  talk good about apple's macbooks and  overall products and that's been  happening ever since we started working  for apple insider many years ago  covering all of these apple products and  especially when apple made the  announcement of the transition to apple  silicon  i was probably the biggest fan of apple  silicon i was telling people this is  going to be a revolution that is going  to end up killing x86 and everybody who  just laughed at me said it's not true  there's no way these new a14x or m1 max  are going to be that good but then they  came out and they ended up being amazing  so many people bought the m1 laptops and  we were recommending the m1 macbook air  to basically everybody and then we had  the hype and the rumors for the m1x  which turned out to be m1 pro and m1 max  and i was saying that those are going to  be the best laptops ever made and so  many people called me an apple fanboy  they said i have no idea what i'm  talking about and then the 14 and 16  inch macbook pros came out and people  were blown away apple really did a great  job with those laptops they made sure  every part of it was a nice upgrade and  still to this day there are people that  are saying on twitter that yes this is  the best laptop ever made but now we  have the m2 macbook pro so let me start  the story of everything that happened  from the beginning when we first got the  m2 macbook pro in we decided to do a  benchmarks video and within that video  we actually tested the ssd and we  noticed that it was pretty slow compared  to the previous m1 macbook pro model and  we pointed out that this could actually  lead to slower virtual memory swap  performance now we didn't actually test  that until the next day when we came in  we tested it out and we saw oh man look  at that it is actually leading to worse  performance so we did a test where we  compared it to the m1 macbook pro and we  noticed that if you have 10 chrome tabs  open just 10 chrome tabs which is pretty  common i would say we noticed that we  were getting worse performance than the  previous m1 macbook pro and the reason  that was happening was because these new  m2 macbook pro specifically the base  model which i would argue is very  popular because that's mostly what apple  stores on their actual shelves in the  apple store as well as what's popular on  amazon as you can see it was ranked  number 20 compared to the 512 gig model  which is ranked about 60 or 70 so the  base model is more popular but on that  base model it would only come with a  single nand chip instead of using up  both of these spots compared to the  previous one macbook pro and the m1  macbook air which would use both of  those spots which would end up giving  you double the actual storage channels  going to the storage controller which  would speed up the ssd and of course if  you're putting on a load of ram the  system has to rely on the ssd  performance to use as virtual memory  swap and that basically caused the m2 to  be slower than the m1 and multiple tests  like exporting some basic photos just 50  photos while also having 10 chrome tabs  open or doing the same thing having 10  chrome tabs and exporting a common 4k  video you would actually get a downgrade  with the m2 machine which i think is  inexcusable and i don't think it's right  to be shipping a machine like this to  somebody who thinks they're getting an  awesome upgrade according to apple's  marketing but really in reality they're  experiencing worse performance than the  previous m1 macbook pro so we ended up  getting a lot of requests in our  comments asking for us to buy another  512 gig storage model that still has the  same 8 gigs of ram to just test the ssd  differences alone so we ended up doing  that in inner comparisons we noticed  that with no background apps open no  chrome tabs no other apps nothing the  512 gig model was 15  faster than the base model that is a  huge difference for just upgrading the  storage and let me say we have never  seen that before on any macbook of the  past especially the intel macbooks we've  never seen a 15 jump just by upgrading  the ssd and then we ended up opening up  some chrome tabs and even safari tabs  and yes the base model got even slower  taking a lot longer than the 5 12 gig  model and then we ended up also testing  the 512 gig storage and 16 gig ram model  of the m2 macbook pro and that was even  faster than the 512 gig 8 gig ram model  so it's pretty clear that if you want to  make the most out of the m2 chip and  take apple's marketing to the fullest  and get the best performance you want to  upgrade both the storage and the ram  which unfortunately brings you up to  seventeen hundred dollars which is only  a hundred dollars away from the 14 inch  macbook pro on amazon the sale price of  eighteen hundred dollars now in the past  with the m1 macbook pro we didn't have  those issues the base models ran  perfectly fine because they had two nand  chips for the ssd so the virtual ram  swap worked great and we could actually  recommend the base models of the m1 air  and the m1 macbook pro with no issues  but with these m2 macbook pros the base  models with only one nand chip they do  have a massive flaw and i do not think  that apple should have gave it just a  single chip i think they should have  eaten the loss and just give it the two  nan chips that the m2 chip needs to  thrive and basically show off that  performance gain that they marketed so  what we ended up doing in yesterday's  video was compare the base m2 macbook  pro for 1300  to the m1 macbook air which right now  you can buy for only 900 on sale brand  new or even renewed on amazon for around  800 so you could potentially save as  much as 500  going with the m1 macbook air and the  findings we found were crazy because  in a lot of the regular apps the common  apps that we tested the m1 macbook air  wasn't that much slower than the m2  macbook pro with nothing else open no  multitasking at all but when we started  to load just five chrome tabs in the  background  the m2 macbook pro was slower in every  single test  not only that we ended up opening  another app in the background which is  pretty common i'd say to have five tabs  and an extra app running in the  background that's nothing crazy that's  nothing extreme this is common use we  ended up showing some huge  differences in the performance but we  also  ended up going to the web browser during  an export which is pretty normal because  if you're exporting video or you're  exporting photos you're not going to sit  there staring at it for a couple minutes  you're gonna go browse the web just like  normal people do and we noticed that yes  the m2 macbook pro was less responsive  when switching tabs than the m1 macbook  air so basically if you're doing any  kind of multitasking at all the m1  macbook air was faster and i think that  is inexcusable from apple to do that ssd  setup with only one nand chip and i  think it's a huge problem but now i want  to talk about the other issue which i  don't think is a big deal but it ended  up blowing up like crazy and that is the  whole thing with the thermal throttling  well we ended up testing the m2 macbook  pro to the 14-inch m1 pro macbook pro  and we decided to run some video editing  tests but we didn't want to run a bunch  of them so we did one easy test which  was the hebc test and we decided to do a  hard test one that we've done for years  we've done it with the 14 and 16 inch  macbook pros we've done it with the mac  pro we did it with the mac studio this  is actually a real world test that we've  done in the past so we wanted to test it  on the m2 macbook pro and we discovered  some crazy results where we got up to  108 degrees celsius and the fan was  maxed out at 7 200 rpm so it basically  couldn't keep itself cool and it had to  thermal throttle severely from an  average package power of almost 30 watts  down to 7 watts instantly because that's  the only way it could cool itself down  and the reason this happened with that  test is because it fully maxes out the  gpu and almost fully maxes out the cpu  as well so it's not relying on the  encoders and that's what makes it  extreme because if you're just running a  100 cpu workload you're not going to  experience that thermal throttling if  you're just running a 100 gpu workload  for graphics you're not going to  experience it and the average consumer  is not going to experience it as well so  when i made my twitter thread about the  severe thermal throttling it ended up  blowing up and a lot of people ended up  sharing it and not even reading the full  thing just reading the headline and  going everywhere commenting that the m2  macbook pro has crazy overheating  problems no matter what you do or in  regular tasks which is not true i was  showing off that one test where we saw  the thermal throttling and i made a big  deal about it because the m1 macbook pro  there was no thermal throttling in that  same test we ran it and it was able to  stay at 100 gpu non-stop no throttling  at all and the 14 inch also had no  thermal throttling it didn't even have  to max out the fans to cool it down so  unfortunately that tweet ended up  blowing up and people didn't read the  context they didn't read lower down when  i said that this is an extreme test that  a lot of people won't really be doing on  the everyday so most people will not run  into this overheating problem but my  main point of that twitter thread was  that  what is this going to mean for the m2  macbook air that does not have any fan  cooling at all it's completely fanless  what's this going to mean is it going to  thermal throttle under other workloads  that are more realistic and more common  that was my point but unfortunately  everything went out of hand i ended up  replying and arguing which i think i  shouldn't have done so i want to say i'm  going to try to be less negative and try  to be more peaceful on twitter with all  you guys that's the change that i'm  going to try to make in the future so  with that said i really wish that there  was less attention on the thermal  throttling thing because i feel like  everybody's talking about that because  it's easier to refute that thermal  throttling claim compared to the actual  issue the big issue with the m2 macbook  pro which is the single nand ship which  is actually causing regular common  workloads to be slower than the m1  macbook air which i think should not  happen under any circumstance whatsoever  no matter if it's five chrome tabs 10  multiple apps this should not be  happening at all and that is what i wish  apple would address and respond to and i  really hope the m2 macbook air does not  have that same issue so there you guys  go that was my explanation of the m2  macbook pro drama straight from the  heart no teleprompter and if you have  any thoughts or questions on this let me  know down in the comment section below  and if you want to subscribe go ahead  and do that right there because we are  going to be testing the m2 macbook air  in depth like we always do actually  running the real world tests instead of  just sharing our opinion and i think you  guys value that so thanks for watching  and we'll see you in the next video

